**How it works:** The Dirty Pipe vulnerability arises when multiple processes share the same pipe descriptor but don't synchronize their use. If one process writes to the pipe while another reads from it, the reader may receive data written by the writer. This is exploitable because it bypasses typical access controls that protect pipes.

**Important notes:**
